 "why_no_result_changes": "the amended FreshSeed changes only where the log sizes come from: for the 10 records version 8's wrapper overwrote it uses the gate's sizes (500, 200, 300), which fresh_seed_data used to make them, and a record that holds three positive integers is used as written; the recorder and the stall slope still come from the record, as before. Every phase that rebuilds a fresh seed requires the rebuilt log's hashes and both removals' hashes to equal the record's; every phase that trains on the training file also requires its SHA-256, its leak check and the four prepared-row hashes to equal the record's (the full-log critic trains on the whole log, which the first check covers). So each phase gets the data its data record describes, bit for bit, or stops. The 10 failed attempts are not stops and make no seed or learner fail; they run again as attempt 2, and no phase's work depends on its attempt number",
